188
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,280
They're just kids!

189
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:22,040
Dammit, how did those little pets sneak through the gate again?

190
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:24,080
I've had enough of their antics for a lifetime!

191
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,780
Don't let them get away!

192
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,280
I don't care if they're kids!

193
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,420
They belong in a damn jail!

194
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:33,740
Did they realize they were on the fourth floor?

195
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,800
Because that is a long fall!

196
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:40,620
The window is a mess, but we lost 26 bowls of ramen, too!

197
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,100
Sir, look at this!

198
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,600
Those kids left a weird note!

199
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,160
Ah!

200
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,340
What is a treasure tab?

201
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:51,480
Sabo!

202
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:55,720
Oh?

203
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:57,380
Wait!

204
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:58,600
Sabo?

205
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,660
I can't believe it's him!

206
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,720
Please come back!

207
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,660
It's you!

208
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:03,720
You're alive!

209
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,500
Let's go home!

210
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:08,700
The hell is this?

211
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,640
Are you friends with that old dude, Sabo?

212
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,520
I think he knows you!

213
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,800
He's confusing me with someone else, that's all!

214
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:15,540
Sabo?

215
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:17,800
No!

216
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:18,760
Sabo!

217
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:19,460
Come back!

218
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:31,540
Sabo!

219
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:40,820
Sabo!

220
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:56,960
You're wrong. I'm not hiding anything.

221
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:00,460
Oh, that's cool then.

222
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:04,820
Come on, how stupid can you get? He's full of it.

223
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:08,620
Damn it, Szabo. We can't keep secrets from each other.

224
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:11,500
So, talk.

225
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:17,760
There's nothing for me to tell you.

226
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
You trying to pick a fight with me? Spit it out already.

227
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,800
Okay, okay, just stop killing me.

228
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,680
The son of a noble.

229
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,680
Who is?

230
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,140
I am.

231
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:38,180
Hmm. So?

232
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,980
If you don't care, then why didn't you ask me?

233
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:46,940
The truth is, both my parents are still alive.

234
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,980
So yeah, I'm not an orphan.

235
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,560
That means I lied about growing up in Grey Terminal, too.

236
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,740
And that guy who was calling out to me?

237
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:58,340
That was my dad.

238
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:04,240
I'm sorry. I know I've been lying to you guys for a long time now.

239
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,500
Well, he said he's sorry, so we gotta forgive him.

240
00:15:07,620 --> 00:15:10,300
I'm not forgiving anyone till I hear the whole story.

241
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:15,600
If you're really from a noble family, why would you want to live in some crappy junk heap?

242
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:20,480
Because I ran away from home, that's why.

243
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:27,900
You understand, don't you, Sabo?

244
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:31,640
A noble must be a gentleman.

245
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,320
Educated, well-mannered, and wise.

246
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:38,480
And then, when you're older, you can marry a girl from a royal family.

247
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,800
That will make Mommy and Daddy very happy.

248
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:43,320
Of course, I'm sure you'll be very happy, too.

249
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:46,920
All I have to do is study and meet the right girl?

250
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:49,740
Then everybody will be happy as long as we live?

251
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:52,020
Hmm. If you work very hard at it.

252
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,960
Good boy, Sabo.

253
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:55,620
Okay.

254
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:58,880
I'll do my best.

255
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:01,120
That's ridiculous!

256
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:03,780
What do you mean the cargo ship's sunk?

257
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,960
I don't give a damn about the crew!

258
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:08,620
Most supplies weren't cheap, you know!

259
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,860
Someone will pay for this!

260
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,900
Hello? Hello?

261
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,280
Calic?

262
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,440
I cannot afford this.

263
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,480
What a mess.

264
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,240
Hey, Dad.

265
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:23,880
Look at this.

266
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,060
I drew it for you.

267
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:35,800
Your father is having a trying day at work, Sabo.

268
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:39,020
If you have time to draw this, you have time to study.

269
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,340
Hey, you!

270
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,620
I'm from the royal family.

271
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:57,300
And that means you have to do everything I say.

272
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,340
Carry me back to my house.

273
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:06,980
How dare you!

274
00:17:07,340 --> 00:17:10,900
I'm related to the king, and I want to piggyback ride right now!

275
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,800
Stop! Get off of me!

276
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:13,340
Huh?

277
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:13,760
Ugh!

278
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:22,300
You nobles think you're so hot, don't you?

279
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,540
This ought to teach you!

280
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:35,920
My son has royal blood!

281
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:38,640
I won't stand for you spilling it on the pavement, you old!

282
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:39,720
Sabo!

283
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:42,760
Tell me you didn't get in a fight with this boy from the royal family!

284
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:45,140
Well, kind of.

285
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:48,540
I mean, he attacked me with this scary knife, so...

286
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:56,920
My son can be such a little beast.

287
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,140
I blame myself.

288
00:17:58,260 --> 00:17:59,500
I do hope you aren't hurt!

289
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:01,300
It's terrible, I know.

290
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,380
Please forgive us.

291
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,840
I assure you, he will be punished severely for this.

292
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:07,020
I'll do anything I can to make things right.

293
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:10,000
Shall we go to the doctor to make sure your son isn't injured?

294
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:21,200
Then I realized, they love their money, their property, their status, but not their son.

295
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:28,180
If I couldn't marry into a royal family, I was useless to them.

296
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:31,400
They tried to teach me culture and literature and all that stuff.

297
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:36,300
But I guess I didn't learn fast enough, because they were always arguing and getting mad.

298
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:39,640
That family had no place for someone like me.

299
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:45,000
I know you guys have it worse, but even if I had parents, I was still alone.

300
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:51,300
I heard that you've been sneaking out behind my back, going goodness knows where.

301
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:56,820
I shouldn't have to tell you this, but stay away from Grey Terminal if you know it's good for you.

302
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,400
We nobles are privileged to live in Hightown with the king and his family.

303
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,140
It's a life the people down there can only dream of.

304
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:08,240
By the same token, you do not belong in their world.

305
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,540
What, you again?

306
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:28,520
I don't know where your parents are, but someone's going to string you up by those suspenders of yours if you keep hanging around here.

307
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:32,640
Please tell me another story!

308
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:37,920
I want to hear about all the different countries you've seen, and about all your adventures on the high seas!

309
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,120
Huh?

310
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,480
You're a weird kid, but I'll give you a pass.

311
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:45,900
Yeah, take a seat.

312
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:46,500
Okay!

313
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:53,140
Well, at least the people in Grey Terminal know what it means to be free.

314
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:58,020
If the nobles in Hightown didn't spend their whole lives licking the boots of the royal family,

315
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,520
maybe they'd look up and see that there's more to the world.

316
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,720
Man, I had no idea.

317
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:06,440
Ace, Luffy, listen!

318
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:10,160
The three of us, we're going to leave this country.

319
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:13,640
We're going to sail the seas and see the world.

320
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:17,980
And once I've done it all, I'm going to write a book for kids like me!

321
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:22,400
Because studying is fun when you're learning about adventure, and we're going to have lots of them!

322
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,060
We're going to be pirates!

323
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:33,640
You don't got to tell me. I'm going to be a pirate anyway.

324
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:38,000
I'll be so tough that all the other pirates and all the marines will bow at my feet.

325
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,940
Everyone in the world will know my name.

326
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:43,600
That's going to be the legacy I leave behind when I die.

327
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,640
I don't care if people hate me.

328
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,940
I don't care if they wish I'd never been born.

329
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,520
But they won't ignore me.

330
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:53,680
That's what it means to be strong, to be a great pirate.

331
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:56,700
I won't ever lose, and I won't ever run away.

332
00:20:56,980 --> 00:21:00,160
Who cares if the world fears me or respects me or whatever?

333
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:01,900
I'm going to be a legend.

334
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,420
Then I know what I'm going to be, too!

335
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:12,020
The King of the Pirates!

336
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:23,560
You dork. Just got to try and show me up, don't you?

337
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:29,960
I don't know if you'll be a king or not, but you're going to do something crazy.

338
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:31,280
I know that much for sure.

339
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:35,320
We all want to be pirates together, though, don't we?

340
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:39,000
We're only saving for one ship, but what if all three of us want to be captain?

341
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Damn it, I never thought of that.

342
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:45,480
Sabo, I always figured you'd be the navigator on my ship.

343
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,080
You guys are welcome to join my crew.

344
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,400
No thanks!

345
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:52,520
But I was nice about it and everything.

346
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:55,300
Also, I'm going to be the king, so I've got to be the boss.

347
00:21:55,380 --> 00:21:56,880
Who wants a crybaby captain?

348
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:57,740
Not me.

349
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,600
Me neither.

350
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,880
What did you call me?

351
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:01,940
Whatever.

352
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:04,000
You gave up.

353
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,980
Man, you're always good for a laugh, aren't you?

354
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:14,800
Well, we'll figure it out when the time comes.

355
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:17,780
Maybe we'll leave on one ship and maybe we'll leave on three.

356
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:22,360
Oh, you stole that from Dadan, huh?

357
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,740
Let me tell you guys a secret.

358
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:30,360
All it takes to become brothers is to share some sake.

359
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:31,900
Whoa, really?

360
00:22:32,340 --> 00:22:33,420
That's so cool!

361
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:37,460
We may sail in different seas, with different crews on different ships.

362
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:41,420
But wherever we go and whatever adventures we have,

363
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:44,860
we'll always be brothers and nobody can take that away.

364
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:50,720
From now on, we're honest-to-goodness brothers.

365
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:52,380
Cheers to that!

366
00:22:54,740 --> 00:23:00,040
Brothers!

367
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:14,160
The antics of Luffy and his friends began to test Dadan's patience,

368
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:18,820
and when Garp unexpectedly pays a visit, the situation becomes desperate.

369
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:21,000
Determined to stay on their path,

370
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:24,280
the three boys must learn to stand on their own two feet.

371
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:26,240
On the next, One Piece.

372
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:28,480
Leaving the Dadan family for good?

373
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:30,620
The kids' hideout has been built.

374
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,780
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

